diagnosis_text:
Affected component: OSPF on the Distribution Switch A pair, specifically the OSPF adjacency over VLAN 99 (br0.99) between dswa1 and dswa2. Mechanism: dswa1 briefly originated OSPF Hellos on br0.99 with a /32 netmask (taken from the anycast gateway VIP 10.0.0.1/32) instead of the subnet mask /28 of the SVI. dswa2 rejected these Hellos with “NetworkMask mismatch,” dropping the adjacency and triggering a short routing reconvergence. Evidence: dswa2’s FRR log repeatedly reports “Packet 10.0.0.79 [Hello:RECV]: NetworkMask mismatch on br0.99… configured prefix length is 28, but hello packet indicates 32” at 00:25:15, :26, :36, :46, :56, :06, before finally forming Full at 00:25:48. On dswa1, br0.99 carries both 10.0.0.2/28 
